REPRO
  karr --dir /path/to/repo          # no subcommand, space-separated value
  => dies "Unknown command: /path/to/repo" (exit 2)
  karr --dir=/path/to/repo          # equals form
  => works, renders that board

ROOT CAUSE
The unknown-command guard in App::karr::execute (from task #5) greps raw
$args_ref for non-dash tokens; MooX::Cmd echoes the parsed --dir value back
as a bare token. The positional_args extractor from task #13 already solves
exactly this (dir has format=s in _options_data via Role::BoardDiscovery since
task #14) — the root guard just predates it.

FIX DIRECTION: one-liner — use $self->positional_args($args_ref) in the guard
instead of the raw grep. Fails loud today (not silently wrong), hence low.

